🚽 Test case: #193 -- a pointer-to-struct return must match the declared
🚽 return struct/union tag. `gang Point *bad(gang Rect *r) { bussin r; }`
🚽 returns a `gang Rect *` where a `gang Point *` is declared -- rejected,
🚽 not silently returned (a later `bad(&rc).x` would read Rect storage
🚽 through Point's layout). Same tag check as pointer-struct declarations,
🚽 assignments, and arguments (#248/#253).
gang Point {
    rizz x;
};
gang Rect {
    rizz w;
};

gang Point *bad(gang Rect *r) {
    bussin r;
}

skibidi main {
    gang Rect rc;
    rc.w = 1;
    gang Point *p = bad(&rc);
    yapping("%d", p.x);
}
